    <title>THE RED ARMY EP 02</title>
    <sub-title>THE COLD WAR</sub-title>
    <desc>Despite its wartime triumph, the Red Army fell from grace. Khrushchev revived it during the Cold War, but purely to crush uprisings by force, even as Soviet science raced ahead with nuclear weapons and the space program. After the Cuban Missile Crisis, it fought proxy wars around the world. By the 1970s, soldiers' lives grew harder, and the long war in Afghanistan helped break the Soviet system. When the USSR collapsed in 1991, the army became a symbol of memory and pride.</desc>
    <icon src="https://tvpnlogopus.samsungcloud.tv/platform/image/contents/vc/00/LINEAR/IN_USQT620324A_3626114792_0_20261016T152700364Z_1_imageprocessorclient-tvplus-linear-6b56cc9f55-cvmx2.jpeg" />
    <rating>
      <value>NA</value>
    </rating>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="IN8000186A" start="20261031114457 +0000" stop="20261031125957 +0000">
    <title>THE RED ARMY EP 01</title>
    <sub-title>THE GREAT PATRIOTIC WAR</sub-title>
    <desc>Founded by Trotsky in 1918 amid total war, the Red Army abandoned its democratic ideals to crush civil uprisings. Fearing its power, Stalin launched the Great Terror of 1937-38, purging its officers. Weakened, the army nearly collapsed when Germany invaded in 1941. Only Zhukov's leadership, fierce resistance, and Allied support carried it to Berlin, uncovering death camps along the way.</desc>
    <icon src="https://tvpnlogopus.samsungcloud.tv/platform/image/contents/vc/00/LINEAR/IN_USQT620324A_3626114792_0_20261016T152700364Z_1_imageprocessorclient-tvplus-linear-6b56cc9f55-cvmx2.jpeg" />
    <rating>
      <value>NA</value>
    </rating>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="IN8000186A" start="20261031125957 +0000" stop="20261031140045 +0000">
    <title>THE DUPATTA KILLER</title>
    <desc>Accused of killing 16 women but convicted of two, Goa's serial killer, Mahanand Naik, nicknamed the "Dupatta Killer," lured women with the pretext of marriage and later choked them to death using their own dupattas. After 15 years in prison, he may soon be released for good behavior, raising the chilling question: Can a serial killer truly be reformed? Does he deserve freedom?</desc>
    <icon src="https://tvpnlogopus.samsungcloud.tv/platform/image/contents/vc/00/LINEAR/IN_USQT620324A_3298912481_0_20260807T145131490Z_44_imageprocessorclient-tvplus-linear-9468c5484-spbjw.jpeg" />
